WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.011
An installation record should make the
comparison understandable.

2
00:00:04.131 --> 00:00:07.352
For the valve identity check, record the
actual model

3
00:00:07.472 --> 00:00:10.354
and tag, the referenced schedule and the
outcome.

4
00:00:10.474 --> 00:00:13.568
A tick without the required observation
may leave

5
00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:16.760
a reviewer unable to reconstruct the
decision.

6
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.397
Use the approved form and record the work

7
00:00:19.517 --> 00:00:22.752
when performed, not from memory at the end
of the week.

8
00:00:23.372 --> 00:00:25.932
A photograph can support an observation

9
00:00:26.052 --> 00:00:28.314
if the relevant feature is readable

10
00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.963
and its relationship to the check is
clear.

11
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:35.158
Record location, subject and the
controlled evidence reference.

12
00:00:35.278 --> 00:00:37.278
A cropped image of a plate

13
00:00:37.398 --> 00:00:40.342
without the equipment context may be
ambiguous.

14
00:00:40.462 --> 00:00:44.515
Photographs supplement the specified
verification method; they are

15
00:00:44.635 --> 00:00:48.774
not automatically sufficient for every
installation characteristic.

16
00:00:49.394 --> 00:00:53.575
Suppose a handwritten serial number
contains a transposed digit.

17
00:00:53.695 --> 00:00:57.087
Correct it using the approved
documentation procedure,

18
00:00:57.207 --> 00:00:59.255
preserving the original entry

19
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:01.679
and recording the required attribution

20
00:01:01.799 --> 00:01:04.270
and date, with a reason where appropriate.

21
00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.611
Do not erase the original or backdate the
correction.

22
00:01:07.731 --> 00:01:11.336
For electronic records, use the controlled
system process

23
00:01:11.456 --> 00:01:13.931
rather than an untracked replacement file.

24
00:01:14.551 --> 00:01:18.198
Not applicable, not checked and failed are
different statuses.

25
00:01:18.318 --> 00:01:20.730
A check outside the approved system scope

26
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.538
needs a justified not-applicable basis.

27
00:01:23.658 --> 00:01:26.069
An inaccessible feature is not checked.

28
00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:28.770
A verified mismatch is a discrepancy.

29
00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.581
Keeping these statuses distinct prevents a
completed-looking

30
00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:36.114
form from implying that evidence exists
where it does not.
